> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > * sunxi-7.2: fix DE33 HDMI primary/cursor update path (RCQ backstop, phys7 cursor)
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > The v35x DE commits its datapath only through the RCQ and relies on the
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > TCON vblank IRQ to trigger the RCQ arm. On cursor-only atomic flips the
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > devices stays idle and the IRQ does not fire, so the staged cursor
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > pipeline never reaches the hardware (invisible cursor). Follow the
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > sun4i sibling drivers and drive the arm from a hrtimer backstop in
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > commit() when no vblank IRQ is outstanding.
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > Also avoid physical mixer channel 8: its per-channel OVL/blender
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > framebuffer fetch returns black regardless of configuration (VSU
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > passthrough and direct programming both reproduce it), so the X cursor
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > used to render as a black box. Map the DE logical channels as
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > {0,6,8,7} - cursor on phys7 - instead of the mainline {0,6,7,8}.
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > And reorder sun4i_crtc_atomic_disable to tear down the TCON before
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > disabling the vblank, matching sun4i-crtc teardown order.
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > Validated BASE + 7000..7004 apply cleanly; sun8i_mixer.c and
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > sun4i_crtc.c from the series match the working tree byte-for-byte, and
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > the HW cursor on phys7 tracks the mouse on Cubie A5e.
